}, {"t": "_COMPILER", "lp": -0.0001644031290197745, "top": [["_COMPILER", -0.0001644031290197745], ["/compiler", -10.324861526489258]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.00019093191076535732, "top": [["=", -0.00019093191076535732], [" ic", -11.673807144165039]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -0.0003140465705655515, "top": [["ic", -0.0003140465705655515], [" ic", -8.692187309265137]]}, {"t": "x", "lp": -0.0006859270506538451, "top": [["x", -0.0006859270506538451], [" x", -9.052010536193848]]}, {"t": " -", "lp": -0.0010330050718039274, "top": [[" -", -0.0010330050718039274], ["\n", -7.63906192779541]]}, {"t": "DC", "lp": -0.00019391271052882075, "top": [["DC", -0.00019391271052882075], [" DC", -9.948063850402832]]}, {"t": "MAKE", "lp": -0.00017423955432604998, "top": [["MAKE", -0.00017423955432604998], ["Make", -9.795793533325195]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're compiling with Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, not the default GCC.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into broken output.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag by flag:\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` \u2014 **source directory** (where the source code lives)\n- `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` \u2014 **build directory** (where build artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja` \u2014 use the **Ninja** build system (fast, efficient build generator)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nCompile in **Release** mode: optimizations enabled, no debug symbols. (This aligns with the `!debug` option noted earlier.)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install to `/usr` as the root prefix\n- Put libraries in `lib` (not `lib64`, which some distros use)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE"}